<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>A Step-by-Step Guide to Implementing Quality Management</b></h3>
                <p>A quality management solution can help manufacturers manage inspections, quality checks, non-conformances, corrective actions, and quality reporting through connected digital workflows.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Quality Strategy Planning: Identify inspection, quality control, non-conformance, corrective action, reporting, and compliance workflow requirements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Centralized Quality Information: Organize inspections, quality results, issues, corrective actions, and related production information.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Quality Workflow Automation: Automate inspections, approvals, alerts, corrective actions, and routine quality activities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Secure Access: Apply role-based access controls to protect quality and business information.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Continuous Quality Optimization: Use quality analytics, feedback, and operational data to improve processes.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>Key Critical Factors for a Successful Quality Management Solution</b></h3>
                <p>Quality management requires consistent processes, accurate inspection data, traceability, workflow automation, reporting, and user adoption.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Clear Quality Objectives: Define measurable goals for defect reduction, inspection efficiency, corrective action, and product quality.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Accurate Quality Data: Maintain structured inspection results, issue records, corrective actions, and quality history.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Automated Quality Workflows: Automate inspections, approvals, alerts, issue escalation, and corrective-action activities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Traceability: Maintain connections between quality information, materials, production activities, and relevant records.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  User Adoption: Provide intuitive quality workflows and role-based training.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-center m-3" alt="Quality Management" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-center m-3" alt="Quality Management" /></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

