<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Managing Change for Successful Quality Management Adoption</b></h3>
                <p>Quality processes depend on consistent execution. Change management helps teams understand the new workflows and maintain reliable quality data.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Explain the Quality Vision: Communicate how digital quality workflows improve consistency, visibility, and issue resolution.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Engage Quality Stakeholders: Involve quality, production, procurement, warehouse, engineering, and management teams.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Role-Based Training: Train users on inspections, issue management, and corrective-action workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Roll Out in Phases: Introduce quality functions progressively and monitor adoption.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Ongoing Support: Address questions and continuously improve quality processes.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>How to Optimize Quality Management for Maximum ROI</b></h3>
                <p>Quality management should continuously evolve to reduce defects, improve inspection efficiency, and strengthen operational performance.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Define Quality KPIs: Measure defect rates, inspection completion, corrective-action time, rework, and quality trends.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Integrate Core Systems: Connect quality with production, inventory, procurement, ERP, and analytics systems.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Improve User Experience: Simplify inspections, issue reporting, approvals, and corrective-action tasks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Review Quality Performance: Regularly assess defects, trends, workflows, and operational outcomes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Leverage Automation and Analytics: Use automated alerts, dashboards, and analytics to improve quality decisions.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Quality Management" /></div>
